{
  "name": "Auto-compress oversized PDFs dropped in Google Drive, log savings to Sheets, and alert Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Auto-compress oversized PDFs dropped in Google Drive, log savings to Sheets, and alert Slack\n\n**Community node.** This template uses the pdfRest API Toolkit community node (@pdfrest/n8n-nodes-pdfrest), so it runs on self-hosted n8n only. Install it under Settings > Community Nodes before importing.\n\n### Who it's for\nTeams that share PDFs through Drive and keep hitting email attachment limits, portal upload caps, or storage quotas: marketing, sales enablement, legal ops, anyone with a folder full of 30 MB decks and scans.\n\n### How it works\n1. The Google Drive Trigger watches an Inbox folder for new files.\n2. Google Drive downloads the file, and non-PDFs are dropped.\n3. pdfRest runs **Extract \u00b7 Query PDF Info (Metadata)** for the page count.\n4. pdfRest runs **Convert \u00b7 PDF to Markdown** and a Basic LLM Chain (Anthropic Claude shown; any chat model works) writes a one-line description of the document for the log and the Slack message.\n5. A Code node measures the original size and picks a compression level from the size bands in Configuration: files under the threshold are skipped, larger files get low, medium, or high compression.\n6. pdfRest runs **Optimize \u00b7 Compress PDF** at that level and a second Code node measures the result and computes the percentage saved.\n7. The optimized copy is uploaded to an Optimized folder in Drive.\n8. Every file, compressed or skipped, gets a row in a Google Sheets log with description, pages, before and after size, percentage saved, level, and the Drive link.\n9. Slack gets a two-line notice per file: what the document is, and the savings.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Install the pdfRest community node and add a pdfRest API credential.\n2. Connect Google Drive, Google Sheets, Slack, and an Anthropic (or other chat model) credential.\n3. In **Configuration**, paste the Optimized folder ID, the log Sheet ID, and the Slack channel ID. Adjust the size bands if you want.\n4. In **Watch Inbox Folder**, pick the Drive folder to watch.\n5. Create the log Sheet with these headers in row 1: Processed, File, Description, Pages, Original MB, Compressed MB, Saved %, Level, Status, Drive Link.\n6. Activate the workflow and drop a PDF in the Inbox folder.\n\n### Requirements\nSelf-hosted n8n, the pdfRest community node, a pdfRest API key, Google Drive, Google Sheets, Slack, and an Anthropic (or other chat model) credential.\n\n### How to customize\nChange the size bands in Configuration to tune how aggressive compression is. Add a Google Drive move or delete step after upload to retire the original. Swap the Drive Trigger for a Form Trigger to compress on demand, or for a Gmail Trigger to compress attachments. Replace Slack with Teams or email. Swap the Anthropic model for OpenAI, Gemini, or a local model, or delete the describe step if you only want sizes.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1160,
        "color": 1
      },
